TASK-132.4 runtime harness: install the Claude extension from the Chrome Web Store through Detour's UI path
— TEMPORARY, never commit the applied result.

Apply:   git apply .claude/task132.4-install-harness.patch   (touches Detour/App/AppDelegate.swift only, #if DEBUG)
Build:   xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug -derivedDataPath .derived build
Run:     .claude/scratch/task132.4/drive-install.sh <fresh data dir name> <out dir>
         launches with DETOUR_INSTALL_HARNESS_DIR and DETOUR_NATIVE_MESSAGING_HOSTS_DIR pointing at
         .claude/scratch/task132.4/blocked-native-hosts, which must hold SHADOW manifests for
         com.anthropic.claude_browser_extension and com.anthropic.claude_code_browser_extension whose path does not
         exist. The override directory is searched FIRST, not instead of the real ones: an empty directory does not
         hide the real hosts. The harness refuses to run unless both shadows are in the first search directory.
What:    opens the store page in a tab, clicks the "Add to Chrome" button Detour's page script took over (real
         mouse-down/up on the tab's web view), reads Detour's modal install prompt (text + alert-N.png), presses
         Install and OK (posted mouse events; performClick if the modal session does not take them), then downloads
         the CRX again to run CRX3Verifier on it and waits 70 s for the worker's first minute.
Output:  <out dir>/harness.log, alert-1.png, alert-2.png, app-log.txt, db-extension.txt, db-permissions.txt
Remove:  git checkout -- Detour/App/AppDelegate.swift

